# ⚠ **The real ledger, and it must never be committed.** `tools/hand_check.py` copies the
# live database off the phone to check the report's totals against the raw MTN messages. That
# copy is Mutalib's actual financial history: every counterparty, every balance, every
# transaction id. The tool that makes this folder is now in the repo, so the folder it writes
# to has to be ignored here rather than remembered by whoever runs it.
# ⚠ **Every copy of the real ledger, not just one folder.** Pulling the database off the
# phone to inspect or repair it is routine, and each pull lands in whatever directory the
# command named — .pulled2, .pulled_after, .pulled_now. Only the first was ignored, so a
# `git add -A` would have committed Mutalib's actual transactions, counterparties and
# balances to a repo. Caught 2026-09-04. The glob is the fix; a list would rot.
/tools/.pulled*/

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
